{# One post, as a card.

   Shared by the two places that list posts: the hub, which lists all of them,
   and a tag's page, which lists the ones carrying it. They were the same markup
   twice the moment the second list existed.

   What is passed in:

     slug  - the post's address
     post  - title, summary, author, hero, hero_alt, published_at
#}
<li class="airside-card">
    <a class="airside-card__link" href="/airside/{{ slug }}">
        {% if post.hero %}
            {# The alt text is the post's own, written in the file and required
               there whenever a hero is named -- it is what a reader who cannot
               see the image receives instead.

               `sizes` is measured, not guessed: this card is between 299 and
               456 CSS pixels wide from 375 up to 1440, and below about 30em it
               is the column. A `sizes` that lies costs more than none at all,
               because the browser believes it and picks the file to match.

               Lazy on purpose, and the opposite of the post's own hero: a card
               is below the fold on the hub and beside the fold at the foot of a
               post, so none of these is what a reader is waiting for. #}
            <img class="airside-card__image"
                 src="{{ post_image(post.hero) }}"
                 srcset="{{ post_srcset(post.hero) }}"
                 sizes="(min-width: 30em) 28rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)"
                 alt="{{ post.hero_alt }}"
                 loading="lazy"
                 decoding="async" />
        {% endif %}
        <div class="airside-card__text">
            <h2 class="airside-card__title">{{ post.title }}</h2>
            <p class="airside-card__summary">{{ post.summary }}</p>
            {# `datetime` carries the machine-readable form so the printed date
               can stay the short one. #}
            <p class="airside-card__meta">
                <time datetime="{{ post.published_at|date('Y-m-d') }}">{{ post.published_at|date('j F Y') }}</time>
                <span class="airside-card__author">{{ post.author }}</span>
            </p>
        </div>
    </a>
</li>
